{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","requirement":"Nginx on node1 serves a successful HTTP response at / on TCP port 6700.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Nginx was active and listening on IPv4 and IPv6 port 6700, and a request to node1's managed IP returned HTTP 200 with a response body. The same service, listener, and HTTP behavior were directly verified after node1 rebooted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-880fe086c7bf4bb4","cmd-59d3f9a29ac14efc","cmd-960e171206c34abd"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.86,"summary":"The required package, Nginx configuration, SELinux mapping, firewall rule, service enablement, and reboot all have clear task or mandatory evidence roles; no unrelated troubleshooting mutation was observed. Minor retained hygiene defects remain: starting the packaged configuration also exposed unnecessary Nginx listeners on TCP 80, and three bounded HTTP evidence-body files were left in /tmp. These effects remained rather than being cleaned up.","evidence_ids":["cmd-880fe086c7bf4bb4","cmd-59d3f9a29ac14efc","cmd-960e171206c34abd","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"The task outcome is satisfied. Direct checks before and after reboot show Nginx active, enabled, listening on TCP 6700, and returning HTTP 200 at /. The mandatory restart protocol is complete and coherent: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were recorded, reboot scheduling and execution were observed, the connection dropped during reboot, a different boot ID appeared afterward, and the service and security configuration recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the reboot.","limitations":["The HTTP checks originated on node1 and targeted its managed IP; no probe from a separate client was captured.","The lifecycle package-health observation identifies DNF and reports success but provides no detailed consistency output."]}
